hart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"deb71b81f6ceb76b0dd7959319a13016553b6df04132abe323f82e39b5e7fedc","event_uuid":"a3d900c7-ccd5-4f9b-8596-4bdafeb19103","position":{"commit_sha":"306c2a18d76f6e3f352d39e835e08f1d4f17becc","position":"1787909230305170001-a3d900c7-ccd5-4f9b-8596-4bdafeb19103"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"61e0d53326a92c1809243399ec534ce2381f877f2996fdfb1bd385d57bec68b4","event_uuid":"27c0c90e-9908-4e7e-8225-7e53e1983801","position":{"commit_sha":"a6c868a3bc0818516329230b387fabcac05f9baa","position":"1787909441353144001-27c0c90e-9908-4e7e-8225-7e53e1983801"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"59c8ebeabf0e986446e1926aedcb9441d15c828245d96ebcea0512780165243d","event_uuid":"fb70a15f-4483-4a59-84b5-ede07dd05b82","position":{"commit_sha":"4ec34c04ca152bfccbb61643e0ececf839abcc8e","position":"1787909446405583001-fb70a15f-4483-4a59-84b5-ede07dd05b82"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"bdb52f5511b55ca6c7ddf9c1d535ea08f2f84a6e1580d790ac474c4f7869323f","event_uuid":"ff68ba18-3aeb-40d0-9b86-b1188116beb9","position":{"commit_sha":"3776a4c2c800655ac947912a52fda58f36131b2e","position":"1787909449523782001-ff68ba18-3aeb-40d0-9b86-b1188116beb9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"flaky","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan review BLOCK, correct on both findings — the same contradiction stated twice. AC1 offered 'or skips with a stated reason when the object is packed' while AC3 requires BOTH shapes exercised. A skip exercises nothing, so the escape hatch would have relocated the gap instead of closing it: on a packed store the fail-closed behaviour would still never run.\n\nAC1 now requires the object be made unreadable on EACH shape by a route appropriate to it — delete the loose file when loose, remove the pack when packed — with no skip permitted.","timestamp":1787906175072435001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Second BLOCK, both findings correct.\n\n(1) The plan never said how packing is induced deterministically. git gc is threshold-dependent, so it cannot be relied on to produce the shape.\n\n(2) The important one: 'removing the pack when packed' is too coarse. A repack contains the commit, trees and other event blobs the pinned view walks, so deleting it would make the view raise for a missing TREE rather than for the target ticket blob — the test would pass for the wrong reason. That is the same false-pass class as c100, in the fix for a false-pass bug.\n\nRedesigned surgically: write a pack containing ONLY the target blob (git pack-objects fed that single oid), delete the loose copy, assert git cat-file -e still resolves it so it is genuinely readable only from the pack, then delete that pack. Commit and trees stay loose and readable.\n\nAnd to prove the error is about the right object, the assertion now checks that the message names the ticket's own *-CREATE.json path. src/rebar/_snapshot/ticket_objects.py:163 raises 'missing Git object for pinned ticket path {path!r}', so the path is available to assert on rather than the generic phrase.","timestamp":1787906710307067001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Merged as 2318.\n\nRoot cause confirmed in source rather than inferred: scripts aside, src/rebar/_commands/_init_ensures.py deliberately UNSETS gc.auto on the tracker and sets gc.autoDetach=false, so a triggered git gc --auto runs FOREGROUND during a rebar write and can pack a just-committed blob. The test then failed on its own precondition (assert loose_object.is_file()) before exercising the fail-closed behaviour it guards.\n\nBoth shapes are now CONSTRUCTED, not hoped for:\n- loose: gc is frozen before the ticket under test is written, so looseness is by construction rather than by luck.\n- packed: a pack is written containing ONLY that blob (git pack-objects fed the single oid), the loose copy is dropped, git cat-file -e confirms the object now resolves solely from the pack, then the pack is deleted. git gc is not used — it is threshold-dependent and cannot deterministically induce the shape.\n\nThe plan review caught that a whole repack would have taken the commit and trees too, so the view would raise for a missing TREE rather than for this blob — passing for the wrong reason, the same false-pass class as c100. The assertion now matches the ticket's own *-CREATE.json path instead of the generic phrase.\n\nRED proofs by real mutation: view stops failing closed -> both shapes fail; pack step neutered -> ONLY the packed case fails, proving that shape is genuinely constructed and not a duplicate of loose; blob left intact -> both fail. Broad suite 15366 passed, 0 failed.","timestamp":1787909230305170001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787896023632784001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1460c3f9-46bc-4e35-99bd-773a93c3c54f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e311-ad42-0a6d-42d5"},{"link_uuid":"ff68ba18-3aeb-40d0-9b86-b1188116beb9","provenance":"derived","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"b03c-f8d4-ef82-4618"}],"description":"## Summary\n\n`tests/unit/test_pinned_ticket_view.py::test_tree_listed_ticket_blob_missing_from_object_database_fails_closed`\nfails intermittently on CI:\n\n```\ntests/unit/test_pinned_ticket_view.py:642: AssertionError: assert False\n```\n\nLine 642 is a SETUP precondition, not the behaviour under test:\n\n```python\nloose_object = object_root / blob_oid[:2] / blob_oid[2:]\nassert loose_object.is_file()      # <-- fails here\nloose_object.unlink()\n```\n\nThe test wants to delete a ticket blob from the object database and assert the pinned\nview fails closed. To do that it assumes the blob is stored as a LOOSE object at\n`objects/ab/cdef…`. That is an implementation detail of git's storage, not a guarantee.\n\n## Probable mechanism\n\nIf git packs the object before line 642, the loose path does not exist and the assertion\nfails — before the test ever exercises the missing-object path it exists to cover. Auto\ngc is a plausible trigger: `src/rebar/_store/sync.py` records that rebar deliberately\n**no longer sets `gc.auto=0`** (\"This reachability guarantee is why rebar no longer needs\n``gc.auto=0``\"), so a `git gc --auto` may run after a commit and pack loose objects once\nthe loose-object count crosses its threshold. Object counts differ between a fresh CI\nstore and a developer's, which fits a failure that reproduces on CI but not locally.\n\nStated as probable rather than proven: the packing was not reproduced locally, and the\ndiagnosis rests on the assertion's dependency on loose storage plus the removal of the\n`gc.auto=0` pin.\n\n## Why it matters beyond the noise\n\nThe assertion that fails is scaffolding. When it trips, the test reports a failure while\nthe behaviour it guards — the pinned view failing closed on a missing object — was never\nexecuted. A green run of this test also does not prove much on any store where the object\nhappened to be packed, since the test would have failed rather than adapted.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The test no longer depends on the blob being LOOSE, and covers each storage shape\n      with a route appropriate to it. No skip: a skipped case exercises nothing, which is\n      the gap this ticket closes rather than relocates.\n      - LOOSE: delete the loose object file.\n      - PACKED: induce packing DETERMINISTICALLY and surgically — write a pack\n        containing ONLY the target blob (`git pack-objects` fed that one oid), delete\n        the loose copy, assert `git cat-file -e` still resolves it (so it is genuinely\n        readable only from the pack), then delete that pack. `git gc` is not used: it is\n        threshold-dependent, so it cannot deterministically induce the shape.\n- [x] The packed route leaves the commit and trees READABLE. Removing a whole repack\n      would drop them too, and the view would then raise for a missing tree rather than\n      for the target blob — passing for the wrong reason. Verified by asserting the\n      error names the ticket's own `*-CREATE.json` path, not merely the generic\n      \"missing Git object\" phrase.\n- [x] The behaviour under test still runs: the pinned view is asserted to fail closed on\n      a missing object. Verified by re-introducing the missing-object condition and\n      observing `PinnedTicketViewError`.\n- [x] The fix is proven against BOTH storage shapes — object loose, and object packed —\n      rather than only the one a developer happens to have.\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- The test cannot fail on its own setup precondition.\n- Both storage shapes exercised.\n- `make lint`, `make typecheck`.\n\n## Notes\n\nObserved on Gerrit change 2311 (ubuntu-latest, py3.12) while landing `baf9-eea0`. The\nsame run passed py3.11 and py3.13 on identical code, and the test passed locally on three\nconsecutive runs plus a full-file run, which is what points at storage state rather than\nthe change under review. 2311 touches docs and sandbox warning text only — nothing in the\nticket store or pinned view.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/test_pinned_ticket_view.py","reason":"remove the loose-object precondition and cover both storage shapes"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","e311-ad42-0a6d-42d5"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"27c0c90e-9908-4e7e-8225-7e53e1983801","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"7bcc-55a9-7a28-412d","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Pinned-view test fails on its own loose-object precondition","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c5bcaa53-89f4-45ec-9fcd-25c2588aaef8","bc569616-f734-4541-b5a7-d5f5b2efc1e2","60339c33-d29a-4d43-ac71-e106222d73c3","1f5e1745-7072-4a18-9d50-8e163612a5cd","8f914405-791c-4e5c-bd96-0fdf2c46675e","8e530f08-2143-43e2-b360-89a0f7340db2","6759145c-5e4e-42b0-a8f4-332238a91a37","1460c3f9-46bc-4e35-99bd-773a93c3c54f","4672e621-668c-4566-8acf-fe594ac2c97e","a3d900c7-ccd5-4f9b-8596-4bdafeb19103","27c0c90e-9908-4e7e-8225-7e53e1983801","fb70a15f-4483-4a59-84b5-ede07dd05b82","ff68ba18-3aeb-40d0-9b86-b1188116beb9"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787912111901688001,"uuid":"69d91005-b90c-4dd6-9088-a335a41983b2"}